# Model weights are ignored by default, with one deliberate exception below.
src/models/*.onnx
# Deep-verification checkpoints (SyncNet / S3FD), fetched from their official
# sources by tools/fetch_models.py with pinned SHA-256.
src/models/*.pth
src/models/*.model

# EXCEPTION: the YuNet face detector is tracked.
#
# It is 232 KB, and it is the one model the pipeline cannot work without. This
# line exists because a fresh clone otherwise has no face detector at all: the
# file in git was named `face_detection_yunen_2023mar.onnx` (transposed letters)
# while the loader looks for `face_detection_yunet.onnx` and fetched it at
# runtime. The consequence was that any check depending on faces silently did
# nothing on CI -- verified: the caption-over-face check reported no findings on
# any clip in the first CI run because the model was absent.
#
# Tracking it removes a network dependency from a gate that has to be reliable,
# and both files on disk were byte-identical (sha256 8f2383e4dd3cfbb4553ea871),
# so nothing is lost.
!src/models/face_detection_yunet.onnx

# transnetv2.onnx stays ignored. It is a 300+ MB optional shot detector that
# nothing downloads, so every run silently falls back to PySceneDetect. Either
# ship the weights or drop the branch; do not leave it looking enabled.
analysis_*/
test_*.ass
audit_inspection/

# Local virtualenv. Created by:
#   C:\...\uv\python\cpython-3.11.15-...\python.exe -m venv .venv
# Pinned to 3.11 because it must match CI exactly -- rapidocr_onnxruntime
# requires Python <3.13, so a 3.14 local interpreter silently loses OCR and the
# mirror detector degrades to "not measurable".
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Documentation & notes (keep private)
*.md
